{
 "title": "D3(b'): ridge alignment map shrunk toward the IDENTITY instead of zero -- does it floor at arm B?",
 "date": "2026-09-28",
 "docstring": "D3 (b') -- IS \"WORSE THAN DOING NOTHING BELOW ~3,000 PAIRS\" AN ARTEFACT OF SHRINKING TOWARD ZERO?\n\nWHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  LINEAGE_TRANSFER_2026-09-28.md (generated by d3_writeup.py from\nd3_pair_efficiency_2026-09-21.json) says the Qwen2.5-VL-7B -> Lingshu-7B ridge alignment map is\n\"worse than doing nothing\" below ~3,000 label-free pairs, and that this \"is not fixable by collecting\nfewer pairs\".  d3_pair_efficiency.py fits an ordinary ridge,  W = argmin ||Zq W - Zl||^2 + lam ||W||^2,\nwhose prior is W = 0: with few pairs the map is shrunk toward ZERO, i.e. toward sending every Qwen state to\nthe Lingshu mean, which destroys the signal the frozen probes read.  But the two models share one\narchitecture (Lingshu is a fine-tune of Qwen2.5-VL-7B), and the identity map already works -- it IS arm B\n(Qwen's own train-half standardiser, then the Lingshu probes), +0.0490 macro.  A ridge that shrinks toward\nthe IDENTITY instead should degrade gracefully to arm B at small n rather than collapse below it.\n\nThis file is a copy of d3_pair_efficiency.py with ONLY these changes:\n  (a) fit_map solves the RESIDUAL ridge  Delta = argmin ||Zq Delta - (Zl - Zq)||^2 + lam ||Delta||^2\n      = (G + lam I)^-1 (C - G), and returns W = I + Delta;\n  (b) the lambda grid is extended with 1e6 and 1e7 so the label-free selector can shrink all the way to\n      W ~ I (it also records the chosen split's val-MSE and the val-MSE of W = I on the same split, as a\n      diagnostic only -- selection is unchanged: minimum val-MSE over the grid);\n  (c) an explicit 'identity' arm evaluated with W = I for every layer.  That IS arm B and must reproduce\n      restandardised_B = +0.0490 within 0.002, otherwise the script halts and reports the discrepancy\n      instead of the curve;\n  (d) the output carries this docstring, the same reference block, a vs_zero_prior block pairing each n\n      with d3_pair_efficiency_2026-09-21.json's curve (same subsample seeds => same pairs, same val split),\n      and a COMPLETE flag written last.\nNS, SEEDS, pairing key, TRAIN-half restriction, by-image split, standardisers, bootstrap, evaluate() and the\nfrozen probes are identical to d3_pair_efficiency.py.  (The identity arm is evaluated first, so the global\nbootstrap RNG stream is shifted relative to the zero-prior run: CIs differ slightly, point deltas do not.)\n\n  python3 src/audit_2026_09_18/d3_ridge_identity_prior.py <out.json>\n\nRead-only, CPU, 4 threads.\n",
